 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Not necessarily, as long as you take few precautions. Cold air doesn't make you wetter than the sides of the road. Cover them with a clear bin if you have one. Keep a small bucket of warm water by the bike, and dip your hands in before you start. That's the polite thing to do for everyone else. The bus can get very busy at those stops. Just normal tyres will be fine, but watch out for black ice. It looks like normal road at first, until you start to slide.",
